<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:31:01Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Canada will move faster from US reliance as tariffs take effect and Trump response looms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:833c046448f5f99a521b1ead8155dd161c9c6d2e969974230cf24e75836428ab</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:29:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T19:19:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/canada-will-move-faster-from-us-reliance-as-tariffs-take-effect-and-trump-response-looms--f0cf636eb7a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/canada-will-move-faster-from-us-reliance-as-tariffs-take-effect-and-trump-response-looms" /><summary type="html">Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney said Tuesday that Canada would move faster to reduce its economic reliance on the United States as retaliatory tariffs took effect on about $20 billion worth of U.S. goods and the country braced for President Donald Trump’s response. FRANCE 24's Christopher Guly reports from Ottawa.</summary></entry><entry><title>'US Midterm elections tend to be referendums on the unpopularity of the president'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71d69bdeb65fe655c93e8499ef1ad031a534fd6a30e72d0f460a60036275003c</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:30:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T16:25:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterm-elections-tend-to-be-referendums-on-the-unpopularity-of-the-president--66d8de516e55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterm-elections-tend-to-be-referendums-on-the-unpopularity-of-the-president" /><summary type="html">Annette Young is pleased to welcome Michelle Swers, Professor of Government at Georgetown University. She frames the New Hampshire primary as both a major Senate contest and an unusually strong indication of the national political climate ahead of November. While Democrats face a difficult Senate map and cannot afford to surrender an open seat they already hold, the broader midterm political environment might become a referendum on President Donald Trump’s performance. New Hampshire is particularly instructive because its closely divided electorate makes national political currents more visible. Swers argues that Trump’s low approval and the local economic consequences of tariffs on Canada create significant headwinds for Republicans, especially in a state whose political identity is strongly associated with resistance to taxation.</summary></entry><entry><title>US war on Iran: 'Incompetent administration when it comes to negotiations and prosecuting war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43e12a63a5e6d356db0558fb5f36edcf7a6cd1bbd48bd5e38603c20c0b34db8f</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:30:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T16:16:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-war-on-iran-incompetent-administration-when-it-comes-to-negotiations-and-prosecuting-war--1e3a59faed45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-war-on-iran-incompetent-administration-when-it-comes-to-negotiations-and-prosecuting-war" /><summary type="html">Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Barbara Slavin, Distinguished Fellow at the Simpson Center. She frames the war in the Persian Gulf as a mutually damaging stalemate in which neither Washington nor Tehran has found a politically sustainable exit: "There are no winners in this war". Her central argument is that the conflict has created a problem of face-saving as much as military strategy. The US faces rising economic and electoral costs, while Iran confronts shortages, inflation, domestic dissent and intensified repression. Neither side, in her assessment, can plausibly claim success.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rubio kicks off tour in Latin America as US vies for regional influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:387f827cea3c8498546f1310ce411c4e2e9dd0c362ec899444c3d00291299987</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:30:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T05:59:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-rubio-begins-latin-america-tour-in-colombia-to-secure-us-influence--172a56fc9e10.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-rubio-begins-latin-america-tour-in-colombia-to-secure-us-influence" /><summary type="html">United States Secretary of State Marco Rubio on Tuesday arrived in Colombia following the recent election of hard-right lawyer and US ally President Abelardo de la Espriella, and a string of right-wing electoral victories across Latin America. Colombia is the first stop on a tour designed to bolster pro-US leaders and cement influence over the continent.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Canada's counter-tariffs take effect on several US goods as trade war reignites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4dae2b8dd6809f2d897692ecebc2d49eed1789a054e72fdae8472f610776d64</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:31:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T04:03:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-canada-s-counter-tariffs-take-effect-on-several-us-goods-as-trade-war-reignites--78ed840cdcb0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-canada-s-counter-tariffs-take-effect-on-several-us-goods-as-trade-war-reignites" /><summary type="html">Canada's counter-tariffs on billions of dollars in US products took effect Tuesday, as a trade war between the two countries heated up. Ottawa's pushback comes weeks after US President Donald Trump imposed 50-percent tariffs on a similar value of Canadian products, over what Washington deemed as "discriminatory treatment" against US alcohol, automobile and dairy industries.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump threatens to ban Canadian Bombardier jets from US market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e67d35b8c61194ca0e2a4346734d90cc6341bf4bff3e506b3f55337fbc39ddc2</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T02:24:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-trump-ban-canadian-bombardier-jets-us-market--64decde9a947.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260908-trump-ban-canadian-bombardier-jets-us-market" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump threatened on Monday to block sales of Canadian planemaker Bombardier in the United States unless it builds aircraft in the country, escalating trade tensions on the eve of Canadian retaliatory tariffs. Trump accused Canada of “unjust and unfair” trade practices but did not explain how a ban would work.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Polarised Brazil': Lula remains a 'strong candidate' despite challenges of incumbency</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8276f77ad8c59c1b3c3d253e431205f074f53bae3136629bf8feae403fceb85a</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T18:50:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260907-polarised-brazil-lula-remains-a-strong-candidate-despite-the-challenges-of-incumbency--1ebb9580cd60.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260907-polarised-brazil-lula-remains-a-strong-candidate-despite-the-challenges-of-incumbency" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Andreza Aruska de Souza Santos, Director of King’s Brazil Institute at the School of Global Affairs, King’s College London and Associate Professor in Brazil and Latin American Studies. According to Aruska, Brazil’s approaching elections can be viewed through competing prisms: macroeconomic performance and political confidence are moving on different tracks. While headline indicators may suggest an economy performing relatively well, she argues that many Brazilians experience a much harsher reality, shaped by the cost of living and a volatile job market.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Five dead after Amazon cargo plane overshoots runway in Miami</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54e3f3998bb4857ac799f757c9ca7842a178fc2ebd6c93c900bc2de505821bb7</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T10:54:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-five-dead-after-amazon-cargo-plane-overshoots-runway-in-miami--f2cd09f9ff0e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-five-dead-after-amazon-cargo-plane-overshoots-runway-in-miami" /><summary type="html">At least five people died when an Amazon Prime Air cargo flight overran a runway and crashed while landing at Miami International ​Airport on Sunday, local ‌officials said.</summary></entry><entry><title>Amazon cargo plane crashes at Miami airport, killing at least five</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e608d2e004d55a018937525774c3400dc5cad6cc2cb3469e6501f7873f7a913</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T21:59:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260906-amazon-cargo-plane-crashes-miami-airport-killing-at-least-five--0db603298e6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260906-amazon-cargo-plane-crashes-miami-airport-killing-at-least-five" /><summary type="html">At least five people were killed and five injured after an Amazon cargo plane overshot the runway at Miami International Airport on Sunday and crashed into several vehicles, officials said. Miami Sheriff Rosie Cordero-Stutz said there was “no apparent threat to public safety” following the crash.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Culture of fear within US Defence Department: Slow leakage of dissent against the administration'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4f01d463a64f5657eec12e0df1af71bb47a00bfcc443e19cb5bf01582e6ec42</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T15:55:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/culture-of-fear-within-us-defence-department-slow-leakage-of-dissent-against-the-administration--5f477c99c6eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/culture-of-fear-within-us-defence-department-slow-leakage-of-dissent-against-the-administration" /><summary type="html">Catherine Viette is pleased to welcome Dafydd Townley, Senior Teaching Fellow in International Security at the University of Portsmouth. He argues that the turmoil surrounding Pete Hegseth points to a problem much deeper than personnel disputes at the Pentagon: The removal and marginalization of experienced officials, the weakening of professional military education, and the prioritization of political loyalty risk changing the institutional culture through which the US military evaluates strategy and challenges political authority.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms start with North Carolina distributing mail-voting ballots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4268d783d3197d1163b97732d71c9862b722c8ad9b9bd815bdcab0b05fdee5a</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:53:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260904-us-midterms-begin-with-chaos-over-mail-voting-crackdown--b948c78e1c61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260904-us-midterms-begin-with-chaos-over-mail-voting-crackdown" /><summary type="html">North Carolina on Friday became the first state authorised to begin sending out ballots, formally launching the 2026 US midterms as President Donald Trump’s administration fights to impose sweeping restrictions on the practice.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US judge declares mistrial in Lindsay Clancy child-killing case after jury deadlock</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6b5efe67824902c1446f0bc4bccd754a74a12f0a914dc638cbf8f8061339590</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:21:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260904-judge-declares-mistrial-in-case-of-us-woman-who-killed-her-children--609fadb47579.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260904-judge-declares-mistrial-in-case-of-us-woman-who-killed-her-children" /><summary type="html">A judge in Massachusetts on Friday declared a mistrial in the Lindsay Clancy murder court case after jurors were unable to reach a unanimous verdict on her criminal responsibility for killing her three young children. The case sparked a public debate over maternal mental health.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump administration unveils anti-immigration video games</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c58bbceb1b6368413941a2952b7e60529370a602309ec9ba43ff2af3c71020c3</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T14:56:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-trump-administration-unveils-anti-immigration-video-games--e19dcf7f44fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-trump-administration-unveils-anti-immigration-video-games" /><summary type="html">The #arcade #games are unveiled as the #Trump administration steps up its mass #arrest and #deportation programme of undocumented #immigrants. According to recent data, most of those arrested in July by #ICE have no #criminal record.</summary></entry><entry><title>An inside look at Lucas Museum of Narrative Art in Los Angeles</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfb9e80b82068a689a066e2515b1aede70f8112741519429a6a9025517a90d04</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:57:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-an-inside-look-at-lucas-museum-of-narrative-art-in-los-angeles--d22e94d7c5e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-an-inside-look-at-lucas-museum-of-narrative-art-in-los-angeles" /><summary type="html">After years of delays and more than a billion dollars, the long-awaited Lucas Museum of Narrative Art is preparing to open its doors to the public in Los Angeles. The museum, founded by filmmaker George Lucas and his wife, businesswoman Mellody Hobson, will be a new home for visual storytelling spanning the Star Wars universe and beyond. FRANCE 24's correspondent Wassim Cornet reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK reasserts Falklands sovereignty amid Milei claim and Trump comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5054340f592091a07862416a9f949092ce20333e0f993584683d6d46168e444a</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T12:44:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-uk-reasserts-falklands-sovereignty-amid-milei-claim-and-trump-comments--3ec0ef408ae5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-uk-reasserts-falklands-sovereignty-amid-milei-claim-and-trump-comments" /><summary type="html">Britain insisted Friday that the Falkland Islands "are British" after Argentine President Javier Milei suggested the "winds of change" now favoured his country's claim to the archipelago, citing Washington's readiness to reconsider its neutrality in the dispute. The islands' fate returned to the headlines after US President Donald Trump threatened to wade into the dispute, while a British-Israeli oil project near the islands stoked anger in Argentina. FRANCE 24's London correspondent, Bénédicte Paviot, gives an inside look at Downing Street's reaction to these developments.</summary></entry><entry><title>US state of Louisiana in battle over electoral map</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35487e08b1e0f4b75c51f165b99e1935176c862251dafc626be50edae0385382</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T12:03:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260904-us-state-of-louisiana-in-battle-over-electoral-map-midterm-elections--ade161a79150.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260904-us-state-of-louisiana-in-battle-over-electoral-map-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">With just two months to go before the US midterm elections, the battle for votes is in full swing. Our reporter Fanny Allard has been to the state of Louisiana, where a redistricting row is playing out with far-reaching implications for racial equality.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>Argentina's Milei escalates Falklands dispute in sovereignty push against Britain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a404403118cf0631bcd9b58c70a990ee8388faeee0812f9b4f4642a81ed8b6b</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T10:07:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-argentina-s-milei-escalates-falklands-dispute-in-sovereignty-push-against-britain--a5cb7dd51916.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-argentina-s-milei-escalates-falklands-dispute-in-sovereignty-push-against-britain" /><summary type="html">Argentine President Javier Milei said he would sanction oil companies drilling in the Falkland Islands, the British overseas territory claimed by Argentina, in a move which could escalate tensions with London. Milei's comments in a televised national ​address on Thursday came ‌days after US President Donald Trump said he was reviewing the United States' neutral position on the ⁠remote archipelago in the South Atlantic.</summary></entry><entry><title>Deadlocked jury in Lindsay Clancy's children murder trial deliberates for sixth day</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84ee0119df25e57e44b618be2455a6e8f2abc59cab28ea19da1b5428d692d971</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T18:44:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/deadlocked-jury-in-lindsay-clancy-s-children-murder-trial-deliberates-for-sixth-day--4c827f35230b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/deadlocked-jury-in-lindsay-clancy-s-children-murder-trial-deliberates-for-sixth-day" /><summary type="html">Jurors in the Lindsay Clancy murder trial are deliberating for a sixth day in Plymouth, Massachusetts after twice saying they can’t agree whether the former labor and delivery nurse is criminally responsible for killing her three young children. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>US feminist icon and journalist Gloria Steinem dies aged 92</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c788c291574ef264dc2548701d4a869d848bacda9b3cd7c9619933245684fdb0</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:39:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-us-feminist-icon-and-journalist-gloria-steinem-dies-aged-92--49355b9195f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-us-feminist-icon-and-journalist-gloria-steinem-dies-aged-92" /><summary type="html">The co-founder of Ms. Magazine and celebrated feminist icon Gloria Steinem has died at her home at the age of 92. An internationally recognised activist in the fight for women's equality, she spoke out for the legalisation of abortion, same-sex marriage, and equal pay. She began her journalism career in New York in the 1960s. Politically, she was an outspoken critic of Donald Trump, arguing that the US had taken many steps back when it came to women's rights. FRANCE 24's Journalist and host of "The 51%" tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Supreme Court corruption scandal rocks Brazil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5940ad3fad2c30d316e4840322542d90dcb60b7de5a030d5c6077133466694f</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T10:42:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260903-supreme-court-corruption-scandal-rocks-brazil--7aeb729bffec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260903-supreme-court-corruption-scandal-rocks-brazil" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, September 3: There's outrage in Malta after a tycoon was found not guilty of masterminding the murder of high-profile investigative journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia. In Brazil, a Supreme Court justice who was pivotal in sentencing former President Jair Bolsonaro to prison is implicated in a corruption scandal of his own. Plus conservationists marvel after a mating frenzy of the endangered kakapo – a flightless, nocturnal parrot native to New Zealand.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Brazilian justice faces pressure for alleged links to disgraced banker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:badcbcccb2e668b94432b25032fe4fca3d490d1c1d121da447e74a92ffd8d6fe</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T09:59:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-brazilian-justice-faces-pressure-for-alleged-links-to-disgraced-banker--e93cbafa60ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-brazilian-justice-faces-pressure-for-alleged-links-to-disgraced-banker" /><summary type="html">The Brazilian Supreme Court justice who sentenced former far-right president Jair Bolsonaro to 27 years in prison for attempting a coup is facing pressure to resign for alleged links to a disgraced banker and potential conflict of interest. This comes weeks ahead of the presidential election in which Bolsonaro's son, Flavio Bolsonaro, is a candidate.</summary></entry><entry><title>Minneapolis apartment shooting leaves three dead, multiple injured</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b9ae2572bed13855b6ef1b767b371c91f57cde278a82e4fa58ab1cbb3f84f7c</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T00:01:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260903-minneapolis-apartment-shooting--2ad6fd708dd7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260903-minneapolis-apartment-shooting" /><summary type="html">Two people were killed and a suspect died after a shooting at a downtown Minneapolis apartment building on Wednesday, police said. Three police officers were injured, including two who suffered gunshot wounds, and were in stable condition. One victim died at the scene and another at a hospital.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US oversees signing of ‘billions’ in deals between Venezuela and Chevron, ENI, GE</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:637944505a45710280d1f79bc667f4db9a03964a6e42a27ac003409a2fa04b30</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T20:54:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260902-us-oversees-signing-of-billions-in-deals-between-venezuela-and-chevron-eni-ge--2dd06b2f2eb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260902-us-oversees-signing-of-billions-in-deals-between-venezuela-and-chevron-eni-ge" /><summary type="html">US oil giant Chevron, Italy's ENI and GE Vernova signed deals worth "tens of billions of dollars" with Venezuela, US Energy Secretary Chris Wright said Wednesday during a trip to Caracas where he and Interim President Delcy Rodriguez finalised the agreements.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Chevron, Eni commit to expand oil projects in Venezuela under US eye</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d237878506a4390d6c616cadcb24cc1955580fd02bf582862a3acbdd55421f5</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T20:00:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/chevron-eni-commit-to-expand-oil-projects-in-venezuela-under-us-eye--791ac7e4276a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/chevron-eni-commit-to-expand-oil-projects-in-venezuela-under-us-eye" /><summary type="html">U.S.' Chevron, Italy's Eni and other foreign energy producers committed on Wednesday to major project expansions to boost oil output in Venezuela, in a signing ceremony in Caracas overseen by interim President ​Delcy Rodriguez and ‌U.S. Energy Secretary Chris Wright. FRANCE 24's Maya Yataghene reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rare train of cyclones fuelled by historic El Nino make their way across Pacific</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7482714309e4ec24e5e8cba139ddf10045259cecdb6c6d44f79f5a14863c877c</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T19:57:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260902-rare-train-of-pacific-cyclones-fueled-by-historic-el-nino--1757af46c4a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260902-rare-train-of-pacific-cyclones-fueled-by-historic-el-nino" /><summary type="html">Several storms, including Hurricane Lowell and Hurricane Karina, moved through the Pacific Ocean on Wednesday, fuelled by a historically strong El Nino that has already been linked to extreme weather around the globe and is expected to persist through to February.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Who is Trump's Venezuela go-between?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6363c703d42f05121b4eb3d46f8bacfc032261beeb21456d96376ddeb67fdfc</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T10:22:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260902-who-is-trump-s-venezuela-go-between--1ce5b20bf924.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260902-who-is-trump-s-venezuela-go-between" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, September 2: We look at papers' coverage of the shadowy Venezuelan magnate who brokered the Washington-Caracas oil deal. In other news, the Pacific Islands Forum wants to talk climate change, but China's anger at the presence of Taiwan is stealing the limelight. Finally, the Bayeux Tapestry is back in Britain after nearly a millennium, with perhaps some salacious secrets.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>US Postal Service whistleblower warns new system could disrupt midterm election voting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc13c16ecfb9475541eee9eff5abe394f23d37f63b7b805c04f98ee6c0b4b900</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T03:48:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260902-us-postal-service-whistleblower-warns-new-system-could-disrupt-midterm-election-voting--6bc9c04ad4ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260902-us-postal-service-whistleblower-warns-new-system-could-disrupt-midterm-election-voting" /><summary type="html">A US Postal Service whistleblower has warned that a new ballot-processing system ordered by President Donald Trump and due to launch Tuesday could prevent millions of Americans from receiving mail ballots ahead of November's midterm elections.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Man accused of killing Charlie Kirk to face murder trial and possible death penalty</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:520e1652b3327ea0d9cabe36c7f0575eb72b32ff9bbfc1fc8caa1817c19cfe44</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T03:38:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260902-man-accused-of-killing-charlie-kirk-to-face-murder-trial-and-possible-death-penalty--a790c5bffe70.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260902-man-accused-of-killing-charlie-kirk-to-face-murder-trial-and-possible-death-penalty" /><summary type="html">A judge in the US state of Utah has ruled that the man accused of shooting far-right activist Charlie Kirk will face trial for murder. Tyler James Robinson, 23, is accused of fatally shooting Kirk in the neck during a rally at a Utah college campus in September 2025, allegedly because he was 'fed up' with the 'hate' Kirk spread.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>G20 backs final statement despite Russia tensions, China dissent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea5dd448817be7d2df0e0b9660675d3982a52befe899f013a2cc151607f5fea5</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T23:39:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260901-g20-backs-final-statement-despite-russia-tensions-china-dissent--aea5b42db1b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260901-g20-backs-final-statement-despite-russia-tensions-china-dissent" /><summary type="html">G20 finance leaders wrapped up two days of talks in Ashville, North Carolina, on Tuesday with broad backing for a final statement, despite tensions over Russia’s participation and divisions with China. US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said Moscow’s presence had not disrupted discussions, as ministers also grappled with the war in the Middle East, tariffs, global trade imbalances and continued support for Ukraine.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Google Maps changes Lake Ontario to 'Lake America' as MapQuest downloads surge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c3000a2f8a88c5a64ec7dbd2a3e95e0eee702200a7a529fbaee60f066245b6f</id><updated>2026-09-08T19:28:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T19:37:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/2026-09-01-18-44-yes-google-maps-renamed-lake-ontario-as-lake-america--4cab93ba55bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/2026-09-01-18-44-yes-google-maps-renamed-lake-ontario-as-lake-america" /><summary type="html">Lake Ontario is now appearing as "Lake America" on Google Maps for US users, following US President Donald Trump's executive order to rename the lake. Canadians still see "Lake Ontario", while users elsewhere see both names. But the change is far from universal: Apple Maps and MapQuest continue to use Lake Ontario. MapQuest has remained defiant against the move and since surged to the top of the US App Store download charts.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry></feed>
